{"name":"French Winery","hex":"#991133","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"french","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare food by cutting it into strips.","To kiss (another person) while inserting one’s tongue into the other person's mouth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/french"},{"term":"winery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where wine is made.","A company that makes wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Winery","blocks":[{"text":"A winery is a building or property that produces wine, or a business involved in the cultivation and production of wine, such as a wine company. Some wine companies own many wineries. Besides wine making equipment, larger wineries may also feature warehouses, bottling lines, laboratories, and large expanses of tanks known as tank farms. Wineries may have existed as long as 8,000 years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/NorCal2018_-020_Sterling_Vineyards_-_Wine_Barrels_-_Napa_Valley_-S0240208.jpg/330px-NorCal2018_-020_Sterling_Vineyards_-_Wine_Barrels_-_Napa_Valley_-S0240208.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winery"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Lustau_003An2019.jpg/500px-Lustau_003An2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Lustau_003An2019.jpg/1280px-Lustau_003An2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Lustau_003An2019.jpg/500px-Lustau_003An2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sherry winery at Jerez de la Frontera","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALustau_003An2019.jpg"},{"srcset":"ht